# Replicate Legacy Inventory System in ERP V2

This plan outlines the steps to achieve 100% parity with the legacy inventory system found at `https://staging-store.parwestgroup.com/`, as extracted during the research phase.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Schema (Prisma)

#### [MODIFY] [schema.prisma](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/prisma/schema.prisma)
Update V2 inventory models to include missing legacy fields:
- **`Store`**: Add `prefix` (String?), `isHeadOffice` (Boolean @default(false)), `latitude` (Float?), `longitude` (Float?).
- **`StoreInventoryProduct`**: 
  - [NEW] Add `StoreInventoryCategory` model and relation.
  - Add `imageUrl` (String?) or `image` (Bytes?).
  - Ensure all weapon fields (`weaponTypeId`, `calibreId`, `licenseTypeId`) are fully utilized.
- **`StoreInventoryPurchase`**:
  - Add `vendorId` (Relation to `StoreInventoryVendor`).
  - Add `invoiceNo` (String?), `attachmentUrl` (String?), `purchasedAt` (DateTime).
- **`StoreInventoryAdjustment`**: Ensure it handles condition-specific stock (New, Reusable, etc.).

---

### API Workflows

#### [MODIFY] [v2 masters route](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/app/api/store-inventory/v2/masters/[resource]/route.ts)
- Update handlers to support new fields for Stores and Categories.

#### [MODIFY] [v2 products route](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/app/api/store-inventory/v2/products/route.ts)
- Support new fields: category, weapon type, calibre, image.

#### [MODIFY] [v2 purchases route](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/app/api/store-inventory/v2/purchases/route.ts)
- Support multi-line purchases (currently handles single product).
- Handle new fields: vendor relation, invoice, attachments.

---

### UI Components

#### [MODIFY] [ProductsManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/ProductsManager.tsx)
- Expand creation form to include: Category (Dropdown), Weapon Type (Dropdown), Calibre (Dropdown), Description (Textarea), Image Upload.

#### [MODIFY] [MasterManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/MasterManager.tsx)
- Add specialized fields for **Stores**: Prefix, Is Head Office, Latitude, Longitude.
- Add specialized fields for **Categories**: Parent Category, Assignee (Checkboxes).

#### [MODIFY] [PurchasesManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/PurchasesManager.tsx)
- Implement multi-product entry table (Legacy parity).
- Add Date picker, Invoice input, and Attachment upload.
- Replace `supplierName` string with `vendorId` dropdown.

#### [MODIFY] [AdjustmentsManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/AdjustmentsManager.tsx)
- Support multi-product adjustments.
- Add Condition selection per line (Parity with `/adjustments/create/regular`).

#### [MODIFY] [DemandsManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/DemandsManager.tsx)
- Support multi-product demands.

#### [MODIFY] [AssignmentsManager.tsx](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/src/components/store-inventory-v2/AssignmentsManager.tsx)
- Support multi-product assignments.
- Add Product Condition per line.

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npx prisma validate` and `npx prisma migrate dev --name sync_legacy_fields` to verify schema integrity.
- Run existing integration tests: `npm run test:integration:strict-real` to ensure no regressions.
- Add new API tests in [scripts/api-integration-test.mjs](file:///Users/asad/Projects/Parwest-ERP/scripts/api-integration-test.mjs) for multi-line transactions.

### Manual Verification
1. Open the local ERP and navigate to `/store-inventory`.
2. Verify that all forms (Product, Purchase, Store) now contain the legacy fields.
3. Perform a multi-product Purchase and verify stock increases correctly in `StoreInventoryBalance`.
4. Perform a multi-product Demand and verify the send/response workflow.
5. Verify that weapon-specific fields appear correctly in the Product management view.
